  "goodToKnow": "Lateinisch means Latin: die lateinische Schrift, ein lateinisches Zitat. The language is das Latein, still taught at many German Gymnasien, and some degrees used to require the Latinum. Mit seinem Latein am Ende sein means to be at one's wits' end, from the days when scholars spoke Latin. Jägerlatein (hunter's Latin) is tall tales, and Küchenlatein is bad Latin. German has thousands of Latin loanwords: Fenster, Wein, Mauer, Straße."
